  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AYC Capacity Building</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The African Youth Commission (AYC) is an independent Pan-African youth network founded by youth leaders to foster synergy amongst youth and youth organisations on the continent and Diaspora. Officially inaugurated on January 2017 by Honourable Patrick Zhuwao, theMinister of Youth, Indigenisation and Economic Empowerment of Zimbabwe in Addis Ababa, Ethiopia, the network is determined and committed to provide a space and voice for youth and youth organisations to set and drive their own agenda, promote the involvement of young people as key partners in the implementation of the Africa 2063 Agenda as well the UN Agenda 2030 for sustainable development,support advocacy actions on the ratification and implementation of the African Youth Charter, other youth rights-based legal instruments and contribute to advancing the AU Shared Values through a network of locally based youth actors.

During previous planning, covid was not factored in and therefore brought disruption. Funding was therefore reallocated to pandemic emergency activities, and covid became a priority even over the strategic planning. Additionally, the current budget structure is more focused on campaign and advocacy (program-based), and not so much on institutional capacity. However, it becameclear that AYC needs stronger institutional foundations to be able to work better and provide better support toits partners.

AYC will work with representatives from the 8 National Consortiums and 46 country members who support AYC in implementing the programs in the 5 regions of Africa. AYC will manage fully the budget, but the other members of this alliance will be fully integrated into the process and consulted to ensure that the new strategy speaks to the priorities of all organizations involved</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">African Youth Commission</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The African Youth Commission (AYC) is an independent Pan-African youth network founded by youth leaders to foster synergy amongst youth and youth organisations on the continent and Diaspora. For purposes of coherence of its profile and priority actions, The AYC has elaborated a Strategic Plan for the period 2018-2020 with the involvement and contribution of its stakeholders and partners. ThisStrategic Plan currently being implemented was validated and adopted during the 2nd GA in March 2018 in Zimbabwe.The AYC 2018-2020 Strategic Plan synthesizes and articulates the AYC&apos;s mission, values, strategic pillars, and priorities for action over this period.he 3 -years strategy was due for review in 2020, however, due to the covid pandemic, the strategy implementation was extended till 2022. The network is now looking to have an end-term review of the strategic plan for 2018 &#x2013;2020 with a view to developing a new strategic plan for the period 2023 &#x2013;2027. By carrying out this activity, AYC will enable the alliance of youth organizations working under the AYC umbrella to set realistic and coherent plans for the next strategic period, and in doing so it will enable influencing activities across the African continent to further the youth agenda on topics such as climate justice and others depending on what the review will highlight as important highly contributing to pathway one of movement building.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
